# Wave W17-M (Route 106): cairn rock — a dark crag standing in the shallows, near-black blue-grey spires with pale worn tips, the cave-dark island’s register set against the bright town sand, foam collar at its foot, the sea baked in around it (design: Cairn Cave’s dark mouth in the black crag beside town). Route 106’s own rock — the darkest rock in the surf arc.
